The '''Plane of Sky''' is a unique, quest-focused raid zone and one of the most difficult pre-Kunark encounters. Progression through the zone is built around a series of floating islands: each island’s inhabitants drop key components that allow access to the next island.

Most of the best Plane of Sky loot comes from class quests rather than direct boss drops. These quests usually require a combination of common island drops, rarer boss drops, and Wind Runes. For the class quest tables, see the [[Plane of Sky#Plane of Sky Class Quests|Plane of Sky Class Quests]] section.

Plane of Sky is the dominion of [[Veeshan]], mother of all dragons. Her physical form, the [[Eye of Veeshan]], is generally treated as the final boss of the zone. Like the storms above Norrath, the zone and its residents are chaotic, aggressive, and exotic. Plane of Sky contains many unusual creature types and models, including genies, harpies, fairie dragons, and other rare entities.

This zone is sometimes called the '''Plane of Air''' in old guides and by some players. This should not be confused with '''Eryslai, the Kingdom of Wind''', the Planes of Power zone also known as the Plane of Air and home to Xegony. The Plane of Sky’s internal zone name, used by <code>/who</code>, is unfortunately <code>airplane</code>.

